essions by Indigenous creators, the descendants of the earliest European colonizers, as well as enslaved Africans, and the work of artists who came to the United States through immigration, this set of objects from the Weisman collection presents a rich and complex panorama of American art.\n<\/p>","cost":"Free","related_content":[],"location":"333 E. River Road, Minneapolis, MN 55455","location_title":"333 E. River Road, Minneapolis, MN 55455","location_latitude":44.979381,"location_longitude":"-93.236654","location_id":27,"thumbnail":"https:\/\/events.tc.umn.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/517\/width\/300\/height\/300\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1920,600\/3842_more-beautiful-more-terrible-more-various-homepage-1.png","thumbnail_caption":null,"thumbnail_alt":"Artwork from the Weisman's collection","has_registration":null,"registration_owner_email":"susannah@umn.edu","has_wait_list":null,"registration_limit":null,"wait_list_limit":null,"rsvp_total":null,"rsvp_waitlist_total":null,"event_types":["Arts, Culture, Architecture, and Design","Diversity, Equity, and Multicultural","Exhibition"],"event_types_audience":["Alumni","Faculty","K-12 Youth","Public","Staff","Students - All","Students - Graduate and Professional","Students - Undergraduate","University Community"],"event_types_campus":["Twin Cities"],"tags":["Art","Art History","Exhibit","Weisman Art Museum"],"tags_starred":["Exhibit"],"tags_global":["Exhibit"],"last_editor":"Susannah Schouweiler","last_modified":1773258429,"thumbnail:html":"<picture>\n\t<source type=\"image\/webp\" srcset=\"https:\/\/events.tc.umn.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/517\/width\/300\/height\/300\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1920,600\/3842_more-beautiful-more-terrible-more-various-homepage-1.rev.1723745583.webp 2x, https:\/\/events.tc.umn.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/3x\/gid\/517\/width\/300\/height\/300\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1920,600\/3842_more-beautiful-more-terrible-more-various-homepage-1.rev.1723745583.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\